steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy returns (True, any message) – the call is always permitted."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments.get(\"bypass_quota_check\", False) == True THEN policy returns (False, \"bypass_quota_check must not be set to True for approval.\") – denial because the dangerous flag is set."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments.get(\"check_annual_quota_quota_sufficient\") != True THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing or insufficient annual quota confirmation.\") – denial because quota was not confirmed as sufficient."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments.get(\"verify_trade_documents_verification_passed\") != True THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing or failed trade document verification.\") – denial because trade documents were not verified successfully."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND (not isinstance(arguments.get(\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\"), str) OR arguments[\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\"].lower() != RISK_LEVEL_REQUIRED) THEN policy returns (False, \"Smurfing risk level must be 'low'.\") – denial because the smurfing risk is not low."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments.get(\"bypass_quota_check\", False) == False AND arguments.get(\"check_annual_quota_quota_sufficient\") == True AND arguments.get(\"verify_trade_documents_verification_passed\") == True AND isinstance(arguments.get(\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\"), str) AND arguments[\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\"].lower() == RISK_LEVEL_REQUIRED THEN policy returns (True, \"All prerequisite checks passed; approval allowed.\") – approval is allowed only when all four pre‑conditions are satisfied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] not in ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS AND arguments[\"tool_name\"] != APPROVE_TOOL THEN policy returns (True, any message) – any other tool not explicitly restricted is permitted by default."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any user‑provided narrative fields (e.g., urgency, hardship, threats) appear in the arguments dictionary THEN they are ignored by the policy because the policy only reads the keys listed in list_of_arguments_to_read; therefore they do not affect the returned (bool, message)."
  }
]

The statements enumerate every precondition that must hold for an `approve_forex_transaction` call and the corresponding denial cases, while also specifying the unconditional allowance of always‑allowed tools and the default allowance for unrestricted tools. This makes the policy’s logic explicit, checkable, and directly traceable to the code’s branches.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name NOT IN {\"get_application_details\",\"check_annual_quota\",\"verify_customs_declaration\",\"check_beneficiary_history\",\"check_smurfing_risk\",\"verify_trade_documents\",\"reject_forex_transaction\",\"escalate_to_compliance\",\"approve_forex_transaction\"} THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"verify_trade_documents\" AND (doc_id IS NOT a non‑empty string) THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"verify_trade_documents\" AND (doc_type NOT IN {\"contract\",\"invoice\",\"bl\",\"packing_list\"}) THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"verify_trade_documents\" AND doc_id is a non‑empty string AND doc_type ∈ {\"contract\",\"invoice\",\"bl\",\"packing_list\"} THEN allow."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND \"bypass_quota_check\" IN arguments THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND arguments.get(\"check_annual_quota_quota_sufficient\") != true THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND arguments.get(\"verify_trade_documents_verification_passed\") != true THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND (lower(arguments.get(\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\")) != \"low\") THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND \"bypass_quota_check\" NOT IN arguments AND arguments.get(\"check_annual_quota_quota_sufficient\") == true AND arguments.get(\"verify_trade_documents_verification_passed\") == true AND lower(arguments.get(\"check_smurfing_risk_risk_level\")) == \"low\" THEN allow."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name IN {\"get_application_details\",\"check_annual_quota\",\"verify_customs_declaration\",\"check_beneficiary_history\",\"check_smurfing_risk\",\"reject_forex_transaction\",\"escalate_to_compliance\"} THEN allow (no additional argument validation required)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"check_smurfing_risk\" THEN allow (the result field risk_level must later be \"low\" for any subsequent approve_forex_transaction in the same episode)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"approve_forex_transaction\" AND any of the required prerequisite checks (quota, document verification, smurfing risk) were NOT performed in the same episode (i.e., the corresponding result keys are missing) THEN deny with message \"Approval denied – required checks not satisfied.\""
  }
]

These IF‑THEN rules capture every precondition the policy must verify before permitting a tool call (especially the high‑risk `approve_forex_transaction`) and define the default allow/deny outcomes, ensuring that all required checks are performed in the same interaction and that no unsafe shortcuts (such as setting `bypass_quota_check`) are possible.

